 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "c-eq-8-45",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book says the square momentum simply decays exponentially for $\\keta\\kt \\ll 1$. To first order in $\\keta\\kt$, Eq. (8.44) gives $\\overline{\\kpcm^2} \\approx \\overline{\\kpcm(0)^2}(1 - 2\\keta\\kt) + 2\\kDdiff\\kt$: the square momentum falls only for a particle that starts above equilibrium, $\\overline{\\kpcm(0)^2} > \\kDdiff/\\keta$, and Eq. (8.45) holds when $\\overline{\\kpcm(0)^2} \\gg \\kDdiff/\\keta$; a particle starting at rest gains $\\overline{\\kpcm^2} = 2\\kDdiff\\kt$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-eq-8-49",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints $\\overline{\\kpcm^2} = \\kDdiff\\kt$. As $\\keta \\rightarrow 0$, $\\frac{\\kDdiff}{\\keta}(1 - e^{-2\\keta\\kt}) \\rightarrow 2\\kDdiff\\kt$, so Eq. (8.44) gives $\\overline{\\kpcm^2} = \\overline{\\kpcm(0)^2} + 2\\kDdiff\\kt$, and $2\\kDdiff\\kt$ for a particle starting at rest."
  }
 ],
