   "id": "naive-commutator-decay",
   "what": "the decay of the commutator under naive dephasing",
   "source": "Modern Atomic and Optical Physics II, 8.4.2 The Heisenberg-Langevin approach",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "text": "The naive dephasing terms: $\\dot{\\hat\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta} \\sim -\\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta}\\hat\\sigma_{\\alpha,\\beta}$ for every coherence.",
       "src": "8.4.2"
      },
      {
       "text": "A coherence and its conjugate decay at the same rate, $\\gamma_{\\beta,\\alpha} = \\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta}$.",
       "src": "(3.93)"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\frac{d}{d\\kt}[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]} = \\mk{a}{[\\frac{d}{d\\kt}\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]} + \\mk{b}{[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\frac{d}{d\\kt}\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]}",
      "src": "(8.51)",
      "uses": [],
      "why": "The product rule."
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\frac{d}{d\\kt}[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]} = \\mk{a}{[-\\gamma_{\\beta,\\alpha}\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]} + \\mk{b}{[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, -\\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta}\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]}",
       "uses": [
        0
       ]
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\frac{d}{d\\kt}[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]} = \\mk{R}{-(\\gamma_{\\beta,\\alpha} + \\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta})[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]}",
       "uses": [],
       "map": {
        "a": "R",
        "b": "R"
       }
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\frac{d}{d\\kt}[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]} = \\mk{R}{-2\\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta}[\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\beta,\\alpha}, \\hat{\\sigma}_{\\alpha,\\beta}]}",
       "uses": [
        1
       ]
      }
     ],
     "num": "(8.52)",
     "note": "The book prints the rate $-\\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta}$. Each of the two terms of Eq. (8.51) contributes, so the commutator decays at $\\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta} + \\gamma_{\\beta,\\alpha} = 2\\gamma_{\\alpha,\\beta}$."
    }
   ]
